WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.145 --> 00:00:07.020
ABHISHEK KASHYAP: Hi.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.410
In this session, we'll talk
about Data QnA, a new Google

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:16.510
Cloud Service that Veolia is
using to democratize access

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.820
to BigQuery.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.142
I'm Abhishek Kashyap,
product manager for Data QnA

00:00:23.142 --> 00:00:27.240
and BigQuery ML at Google Cloud.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.130
FABRICE NICO: Hello,
I'm Fabrice Nico.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.150
Thanks a lot to Google
for the invitation.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.620
I've been working at
Veolia for nine years.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.950
I'm part of the IT department.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.340
I'm in charge of all subject
related to data and robotics

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.860
object for the group
function support.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.740
And my main customers are
finance, procurement, HR,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.690
legal departments.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.540
ABHISHEK KASHYAP: Thank you,
Fabrice, for joining us today.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.880
In terms of the
agenda, we'll start

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.030
by introducing Data QnA,
which as the name suggests,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.800
is a natural language based
question-answer service

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.340
for getting insights
on your BigQuery data

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.610
by just typing a question,
wherever you are.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.980
We will follow it up
with our discussion

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.560
on Veolia, which will
be led by Fabrice.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.320
Let us start with Data QnA.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.780
As I mentioned, I'm
a product manager

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.320
for BigQuery ML, which is
another product at Google Cloud

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.300
to do machine learning.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.040
We have a product dashboard
for various metrics

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.740
that I need to track to
do my day to day job.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.060
But I do have a lot of ad hoc
questions every now and then,

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:45.000
because our dashboard cannot
contain all the charts that I

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.330
might need in the future.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.980
As I show in this
example, when I

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:53.330
want to know how many on
demand customers used BigQuery

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.410
ML last week, I have to
go find their ticket,

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:02.720
and their developer has to add
a new chart to the dashboard.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.150
That takes almost
two days, which

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.250
delays me in doing my work.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.150
But more than that, it is a
distraction for the developer,

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.880
as they have to stop
doing their day job

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.280
and take care of
this simple chart.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.880
With Data QnA, now I'm
just able to go and ask

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.540
that question using text and
get the answer right away.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.910
And I do not have to bother
the developer whenever

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.110
I have a question like this.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:38.400
So what we are doing
here is democratizing

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.910
access to insights
by enabling users

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:48.240
to ask questions in natural
language on BigQuery data.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.590
When we say democratization,
let us see what it entails.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:57.150
In this case, I could ask a
question in free form text.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.120
I did not have to know the
underlying data at all.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.710
I could just talk in what we
call a business speak, rather

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.540
than data speak,
which is what you

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.300
need for a broad set
of users to use this.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.520
There is information
provided, which in this case

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.690
is an interpretation of
the question that I read,

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:22.310
and that formed trust
for me, in knowing

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.330
that it is answering
what I asked for

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.020
and the answer is correct.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:32.530
Fourth, I can go access it
in that interface I work in.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:35.260
In this case, this
was Google Sheets.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.310
I, as a business user, am
working in spreadsheets a lot,

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:44.050
so I did not have to go open a
SQL editor and type it in there

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.210
to get the answer I needed.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.650
And finally, the BigQuery
governance and access policies

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:56.290
that have been defined are all
taken care of automatically.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.820
There is no chance that
somebody without access

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.760
to this confidential
customer information

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.000
would be able to go and
get access to this data

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.730
from this new natural
language interface.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:18.519
The vision for Data QnA
is for any business user

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:21.579
to go to their interface
of choice, which

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:26.370
could be a chatbot, a
spreadsheet, or a BI platform,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.010
ask a question through
natural language

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.270
and get an answer back.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:36.450
Data QnA parses the
question that is asked,

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.930
identifies the intent
and the entities,

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:45.340
matches those to the underlying
data, generates a SQL,

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.080
and returns an answer
to the end user.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.870
And from this, we see
three key benefits.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:05:00.580
One, any business user
with the appropriate access

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.160
can go ask a question
and get insights

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.260
when they need
it, without having

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:10.010
to wait for somebody else to
add a chart to the dashboard.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.060
Second, the BI
team, which usually

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.770
responds to these ad hoc
requests, can be freed up.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:21.370
And they can focus on
more critical tasks.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:28.960
And finally, we enable access
through multiple interfaces.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.050
So it is available
wherever users work.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:37.500
During the alpha,
this is natively

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:42.210
available through Google
Sheets and BigQuery web UI.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:45.090
We also have APIs,
which would allow

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:51.690
you to embed Data QnA into a
chatbot or your own custom UI,

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:55.760
so you can make it
available in whatever tool

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.360
your business users work in.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.920
Now let us see
Data QnA in action.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.070
We have some open source
data from Instacart

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:10.310
that contains
transaction information,

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.490
along with information
on the items,

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:18.350
the location, and
the member loyalty.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:23.240
We set up Data QnA once,
and we will show you

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:26.540
how you can ask questions
and get insights

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:31.190
on three different interfaces,
a Google chat chatbot, Google

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:37.060
Sheets, or the BigQuery web UI.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.600
The experience on
Sheets is similar.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.840
Sheets has a feature called
Connected Sheets that

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.720
allows you to connect
to a BigQuery table

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.980
and analyze that table through
the spreadsheet itself.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:55.000
With Data QnA, you can start
asking questions on that data

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.240
as well.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.140
In this case, the
UI is richer, and we

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.230
are able to even
auto suggest entities

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.960
that help users get
a better experience

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:08.080
and make less errors in
writing these questions.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.410
To illustrate some of the
more advanced capabilities,

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:15.310
an example question here is
to compare the average price

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:20.580
between two products, which are
values in one of the columns

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.550
in the underlying data.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:27.730
And as you can see, we do return
the SQL as well for a more

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.460
advanced user to validate.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:34.180
And there is a
feedback button, using

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.890
which a user can signal whether
the answer was correct or not.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.870
And all of this
information is passed

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:45.940
in to the person who set up Data
QnA, who can view this feedback

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:50.790
and improve the service
for the end user.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.450
The third demo is
on the BigQuery UI.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:58.800
We have SQL analysts who are
proficient in SQL who usually

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.460
can use the BigQuery UI.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:06.890
However, as you can see from
one of these example queries,

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:10.050
some of the queries
can take time to write.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.610
So we have added Data QnA
as a productivity function

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.280
to the BigQuery UI.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.020
So you can just type a question.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.410
It will generate a
query for you that you

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:25.130
can populate into the
SQL editor and continue

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:27.510
to edit it or run it as is.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.280
To summarize the features that
we just showed, with Data QnA,

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.460
you can ask a question
in free form text

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.860
without having to load
the underlying data.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:44.100
But you can use
business terminology.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:48.810
Using Google knowledge graph,
we understand common synonyms.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:52.470
We auto suggest column
names and data values.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.350
These are available
through the API.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:59.880
We do accept typos, so if a user
makes an error, we do not fail.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.290
We come back with
the right value.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.690
And if we do not understand
the question fully,

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.710
we return a clarification.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:11.080
We are optimized for
precision versus coverage.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.980
So if we are not
sure, we'll just ask,

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:17.150
did you mean x or
did you mean y?

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:22.250
We have a setup that enables
answering incomplete questions.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.270
As an example, if I
just said top products

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.180
and did not mention
I wanted my revenue,

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:31.300
revenue could have been
set up as a default metric.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:36.400
And we will return an answer
just by saying top products.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.740
If your tables are
date partitioned,

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:43.220
we do query the right partition
to optimize the costs.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.760
And for all BigQuery
governments and cost

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.980
controls that you
have set up, we

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.350
will work with those
out of the box.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.300
I mentioned setup.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.560
The reason we have a setup
component is twofold.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.360
One, not all data is clean.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:09.660
So we have many customers
who have created views

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.660
for powering end user
dashboards, which

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:18.190
have their clean data that is
trusted by the organization.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:22.680
Data QnA can be enabled
on all of those views

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.870
and provide the right
answer to the end users.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:32.160
Second, we do want you
to add business domain

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.910
specific synonyms to the
individual columns in your data

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:40.450
so that business users do
not have to ask questions

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.800
using column names, which as
we know, could be anything.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.410
But they can use the
business terminology

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.810
they use day in and day out.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:54.060
Finally, we show reports of
all questions being asked

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.740
and the results as
well as the status,

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.610
whether it was
successful or it failed,

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:03.480
in a dashboard to the person
who sets up these tables

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:05.660
or views for Data QnA.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.660
So you can continuously monitor
these and improve the service

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.550
if something is
not being answered

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:17.250
or if some answer
does not look correct.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:20.970
With that, I will hand
it over to Fabrice

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.202
to talk about Veolia.

00:11:23.202 --> 00:11:24.660
FABRICE NICO: Hi,
Fabrice speaking.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.150
Thanks a lot, Abhi,
for your introduction.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:30.180
I'm here today to tell
you a story about how

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:34.110
we support our businesses
with innovative and digital

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.820
solutions.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:40.050
More precisely, how we reached
the target with Google support

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.630
and a little bit of imagination.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.950
The touch of imagination
is called ISA,

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.600
but we will see this idea later.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.310
For those we don't
know Veolia yet,

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:58.080
we provide services around
three main businesses

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.730
around the world--

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:04.980
water, waste, and energy are
the heart of our activities

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:12.240
operated by 178,000 employees
through five continents.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:15.070
Veolia's mission is
to resource the world.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:18.900
We contribute to developing
access to resources,

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:22.570
preserving and
prepositioning them.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:27.730
An example is 98 million people
supplied with safe drinking

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.190
water, 42 million
people provided

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:33.490
with collection services.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:38.170
Or again, 41 billion megawatts
of power produced per year.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.740
Veolia's strategic program
is called Impact 2023,

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.190
and the objective is to make
Veolia a benchmark company

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:53.070
for ecological conservation.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:56.790
To support this program,
the Veolia IT department

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.610
has started, since
over the past year,

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.990
multiple digital
automation programs.

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:06.870
In example, in 2013,
with [INAUDIBLE] adoption

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.430
for the entire group.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:14.370
Or in 2017, we have digital
workplace setting up

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.160
and public cloud adoption.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.250
And finally in 2019,
with bringing data

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:24.250
value to help businesses.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:28.700
Strong IT foundation, built
so far by IT departments,

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:37.920
support objectives of Impact
2023 strategic program.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:41.250
To be concrete and give you
an example of the difficulty

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.790
we've got within Veolia,
and I think concern a lot

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:47.520
of companies around
the world, I would

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.160
like to tell you a story
about how we can democratize

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.780
the information access.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:56.840
In my previous life,
when I was a consultant,

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.870
to find valuable
information was like to be

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.480
a hunter in a jungle.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.590
If you don't have
the right networking,

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.240
it's fairly an
impossible mission.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.600
And finally, if you
catch it, this one

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:15.480
will be out of date or
only readable by an expert.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:19.100
Offering right information
to do it right population

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:21.855
at the right moment,
it's really a challenge.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.490
Who has never been
upset in meetings

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:30.460
not to get access
directly and quickly

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.650
to your own information?

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:36.930
To the crucial data essential
to the decision making.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:40.050
I think about CFO
who want on demand

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:44.280
and immediately to access to
revenue or every day figures

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.880
for a specific organization.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.030
Or service manager
who wants to find

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.120
quickly his remaining
budget anywhere, any time,

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.970
and from any devices.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:15:00.620
Our dream is to democratize
access to information,

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:06.790
and that businesses are the
owner of their own information.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.790
Information should be
available instantly

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.550
and on demand in a simple way.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.020
And businesses must
be confident with it.

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:23.110
How do we succeed to fulfill
this business agreement?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:26.810
Firstly, thanks to the Veolia
strategy and transformation

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:30.440
atmosphere, management
supported us

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.310
and pushed us to be
disruptive, and above all,

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:38.180
gave us the means and the tools
to meet the challenges related

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:40.630
to help transformation.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:45.220
Secondly, thanks to the training
program and new IT skills,

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:49.030
digital communities have been
engaged by the IT department

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.820
to facilitate transformation.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:55.530
And third, thanks to the
technical tools and partnership

00:15:55.530 --> 00:16:00.190
with Google, platform as a
service and Google advice

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:03.870
sped up the availability
of our solution.

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:07.500
For instance, the
origin of our solution

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:12.120
comes from exchanges with
Google and from another document

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:16.650
dedicated to exploring
data with conversation.

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:19.980
This context allowed
us, in four months,

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:24.210
to offer a new digital solution
based on data lake concept

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.366
and chatbot to our businesses.

00:16:27.366 --> 00:16:29.760
Our solution is
called ISA and is

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:33.760
to democratize and streamline
the access to the information,

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:37.140
in order to optimize the
decision making process.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.640
Our concept is based
on three pillars--

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:45.110
information, self
service, and access, ISA.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.510
Information,
because data is gold

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:50.940
and is essential to
the decision making.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:55.070
Self service to let business
become self-sufficient

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.100
about data management.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:01.360
And access to the information
needs to be implicitly

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.470
simple and quick.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.890
Our ISA solution was put
in live a few months ago

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:11.017
and helped our business to adopt
the digital transformation.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.040
A quick demo showing
how ISA works today.

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:22.210
User asks question
in our chat to ISA.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:25.910
Answer is displayed on a
smart card with a web link.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:28.420
When you click on
that, information

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:32.740
is published in a data
studio, prefiltered,

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.560
showing this information.

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.900
It's really [INAUDIBLE]
to consume information

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:38.690
in a simple way.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.840
And after ISA, what's next?

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.790
We never stopped
our collaboration

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.830
with the Google team.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:53.070
A new solution with QnA
looks like a good way

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:55.840
to upgrade our ISA solution.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.960
This new and innovative
functionalities

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:05.840
will open up a data access view
to 360 degree to our business.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.750
What are the main
functionalities

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:11.170
we tested and we found
interesting to be integrated

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:11.680
to ISA?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:20.280
The first is the
capabilities of QnA

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.220
to offer, in real time, multiple
comparisons and analyses

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:29.370
based on data available from
the data lake environment.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.580
Second one is to
produce in the tool

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:36.050
multiple charts based on
previous analyses related

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.000
to a question.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.810
Benefit for us, if the
app needs acceleration

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.210
of the proposal of
several answers,

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.970
we would configuration
by the development team.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:53.910
All of our great
features are based

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:58.380
on the multiple suggestions
offered by QnA [INAUDIBLE]

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:01.125
as an accelerator to the
adoption of the solution.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:09.720
And last one, but not least,
QnA offers a configuration

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:14.750
console to enrich easily and
quickly the user experience.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.460
And again, this feature
optimizes the time

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:20.160
to configure new answers.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.900
In conclusion, integration
of QnA into our ISA solution

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:29.530
is eagerly awaited in order to
offer our businesses a new user

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.460
experience.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:33.215
Thanks, Abhi, for
this time, and I'll

00:19:33.215 --> 00:19:34.948
let you to carry on
this presentation.

00:19:34.948 --> 00:19:36.490
ABHISHEK KASHYAP:
Thank you, Fabrice,

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:39.400
for providing us
with insights on how

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.885
you are planning to use Data
QnA to extend your ISA solution.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:50.230
I'll wrap up by talking
about the pricing

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:55.170
and pointing to some
resources to get you started.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.950
In terms of pricing,
Data QnA is not

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:02.040
going to have any
additional charge.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:06.360
You can use Data QnA and ask
questions in natural language,

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:11.130
just like you could write a
SQL clearly and get an answer.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.640
The only charge is going to
be for the underlying BigQuery

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:17.590
queries that get executed.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:21.160
And you pay for them if you
use on demand pricing model.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.040
If you use BigQuery
reservations,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:27.200
you can use your slots as is.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.960
When we set up, we
do index the data

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.690
values in the table to
provide capabilities,

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.370
like auto suggest.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:40.430
That does carry a charge within
BigQuery or use your slots.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:52.120
And finally, Data QnA
could require integration

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:59.200
with a chatbot or custom
UI, and you may also

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.900
need some help with the
set up and management

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:07.300
on individual data sets that
you want to enable Data QnA on.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:11.890
We have partnered with some
key Google Cloud partners

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.750
to help you get started.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.770
Please do reach out to them
if you are working with these

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:19.180
to get started with Data QnA.

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:24.770
A next step, if you are
interested in participating

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:29.750
in the alpha, please reach out
to your Google point of contact

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:34.440
or just fill the form
at the link below,

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.540
and we will get back to you.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:40.080
Thank you for your time,
and have a great day.

